 H←DATES PLANETSPOS P;PL;ROWS
⍝ Table of planet positions for multiple dates
⍝ Result is 3D array: dates × planets × coordinates
⍝ ROWS holds, for each date, the planets in P followed by the comet;
⍝ they are joined as the book's loop joins them, by catenation on the
⍝ first axis to an empty table, so a scalar P stacks the rows instead
 PL←Data.planets[,P;]
 ROWS←{(⍵ PLANETPOS PL),[1]⍵ COMETPOS Data.kohoutek}¨,DATES
 H←⊃{⍵,[1]⍺}/⌽(⊂(0,(1+⍴P),3)⍴0),ROWS
